{
  "sourcePatchId": "46336034-3d43-4b9d-af44-ce2715ed747b",
  "name": "Trance Gate",
  "description": "Continuous stereo Trance Gate. CH16 CC24 sets amplitude to CC/127. CH16 CC29: 127 starts a triangle LFO at Start frequency; 0 sweeps back and stops. Repeated 127 holds; other values leave the switch unchanged. On retrigger, frequency and phase restart. Sweep time is the full linear start-to-end duration; early release returns proportionally sooner. The 0–1 triangle starts at zero rising and opens above Threshold. Either CC24 or the LFO can open the gate. Shared Attack/Release half-times (defaults 5/10 ms) smooth the combined gain. Starts closed and never resets shared CC state. Use as a serial mixer insert with CH16 controller Step lanes and Reset Value 0. Leave CC24 at 0 for LFO-only gating. Restart the rack after changing performance controls. Stereo (0–1, default 0) scales channel balance: the current triangle while the LFO runs (including return), otherwise a held noise sample on each CC24 zero-to-positive opening. Repeated positive CC24 values hold the position. Pan holds through release.",
  "isTemplate": false,
  "alwaysOn": true,
  "instrumentType": "continuous",
